# Why the Formula Works

Suppose there are **n friends**.

Take the **last friend**.

### Case 1: Last friend stays single

Remaining friends:

```
n-1
```

Ways:

```
f(n-1)
```

---

### Case 2: Last friend makes a pair

He can pair with

```
1
2
3
...
n-1
```

Total choices:

```
n-1
```

After making one pair,

Remaining friends:

```
n-2
```

Ways:

```
f(n-2)
```

Total:

```
(n-1) × f(n-2)
```

Hence,

[
\boxed{f(n)=f(n-1)+(n-1)\times f(n-2)}
]

